.TH SCRCPYVNC 1 "" "TigerVNC" "TigerVNC Manual"
.SH NAME
scrcpyvncserver \- TigerVNC server bridging scrcpy H.264 streams with zero transcoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scrcpyvncserver
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B scrcpyvncserver -version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scrcpyvncserver
bridges an Android device running
.B scrcpy-server
to VNC viewers using the RFB Open H.264 encoding (encoding 50) without
host-side decoding, color-space conversion, or re-encoding.
.PP
It connects directly to the local ADB daemon (127.0.0.1:5037 by default)
via \fBhost:transport:<serial>\fP and \fBlocalabstract:scrcpy\fP with
\fBTCP_NODELAY\fP enabled, strips scrcpy's 12-byte packet header, and uses
scatter-gather I/O (\fBwritev\fP) to prepend RFB Open H.264 headers directly
to the raw Annex-B NAL payload.
.PP
Connecting viewers must support Open H.264 encoding (50), ContinuousUpdates
(\-313), and DesktopSize (\-223) or ExtendedDesktopSize (\-308). When using
\fBvncviewer\fP(1), pass \fB\-AutoSelect=0 \-PreferredEncoding=H.264\fP
to prevent falling back to Tight encoding.
.SH OPTIONS
Parameters can be specified as \fB\-\fIParam\fR, \fB\-\fIParam\fP=0\fR,
or \fB\-\fIParam\fP=\fIvalue\fR. Run \fBscrcpyvncserver \-h\fP for the full
parameter list.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vncviewer (1),
.BR x0vncserver (1),
.BR w0vncserver (1)
